        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Look back at that automobile recall letter from Lesson 11. That letter seems crafted to lull its readers into failing to act in their own life-or-death interest. In the Second Inaugural Address, Lincoln distances God from slavery as deliberately as that letter distances a manufacturer from a defective product. What kinds of ethical distinctions would you make between that letter and Lincoln's address?",
            "block_bbox": [
                127,
                390,
                784,
                510
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
